      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe as written.\n\n- **Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6,400 mg/day.** That is twice the usual maximum for adults in a hospital setting, which is 3,200 mg/day.\n- **A single 1600 mg dose is also above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose.**\n- At this level the risks of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up sharply. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't remove that risk.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day), the usual maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing\n- **400\u2013600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily**, for analgesia or antipyresis\n- **1600 mg total per day**, for example 400 mg 4 times daily\n\nIf you do want 1600 mg 4 times daily, tell me and add a note with your clinical rationale. I'll enter it with that note, though pharmacy will probably flag it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
